              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the dispute centers on how to calculate deferred payments required under section 1325(a)(5)(B)(ii) of the Bankruptcy Code."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that deferred payments must equal the present value of the collateral, which they say is an objective concept reflecting the real interest rate and inflation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Brunstad, respondent argues that a secured creditor in a Chapter 13 cramdown is not seeking profit but merely trying to mitigate the large losses it would otherwise suffer."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Brunstad, respondent also points to studies indicating that the success rate of Chapter 13 plans is low, with failure rates as high as 97 percent in some jurisdictions."
      }
    ],
